# OnStandard landing site — response headers (Cloudflare Workers static assets).
#
# The site had NO _headers file at all until the 2026-07-30 security audit (finding #10), while
# web/admin/ has had one for a while. That meant the public site — including /reset, which handles
# a live password-recovery session — shipped with no framing protection, no MIME-sniff protection
# and no CSP.
#
# Syntax: a path pattern, then indented `Header: value` lines. Later, more specific blocks add to
# (they do not replace) the ones above them.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=()

# The password-reset page. Everything here is deliberately tighter than the rest of the site:
#   · DENY, not SAMEORIGIN — a reset form must never be framable, by anyone, ever (clickjacking a
#     "set new password" submit is the whole attack).
#   · no-store — the page transits a recovery token in the URL fragment; nothing about it should
#     sit in a shared cache or a back/forward cache.
#   · a real CSP with NO third-party origin. supabase-js is vendored at ./js/vendor/supabase.js
#     (finding #3); if someone re-introduces a CDN <script>, this makes it fail closed instead of
#     quietly working. 'unsafe-inline' on script-src is required because the page's logic is an
#     inline <script> block — worth revisiting by moving it to a file, but not in this pass.
/reset*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Cache-Control: no-store
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; connect-src https://ftwrvylzoyznhbzhgism.supabase.co; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'

# The public trainer page: takes payment through public-offer-checkout, so it needs the Supabase
# REST + Functions origins in connect-src and nothing else. Framable nowhere.
/t*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; connect-src https://ftwrvylzoyznhbzhgism.supabase.co https://ftwrvylzoyznhbzhgism.functions.supabase.co; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer

# The private beta feedback board. Reached only with a ?k= token, so:
#   · no-store + no-referrer — the URL IS the credential; it must not sit in a shared cache, and it
#     must never leak to a third party through the Referer header on an outbound click.
#   · noindex is also set as a meta tag on the page itself; this is the belt to that's braces.
#   · connect-src is the Functions origin only. The page talks to beta-board over plain fetch and
#     loads no supabase-js at all, so it needs nothing else. Fonts are local (font-src 'self') —
#     a Google Fonts <link> here would fail closed rather than quietly work.
/beta*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Cache-Control: no-store
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; connect-src https://ftwrvylzoyznhbzhgism.supabase.co https://ftwrvylzoyznhbzhgism.functions.supabase.co; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'

# The per-tester demo-account handout. Reached only with a ?k= token and hands out LIVE prod
# passwords, so it gets the same posture as /beta* — plus a TIGHTER connect-src, since this page
# never talks to the REST origin, only the tester-claim function:
#   · no-store + no-referrer — the URL IS the credential.
#   · noindex — belt to the meta tag's braces.
#   · fonts are local (font-src 'self') — same reasoning as /beta*.
# NOTE: the pre-existing /t* block above (trainer page) also prefix-matches /tester* — both blocks
# apply here, "more specific adds to, not replaces" per this file's header. Benign today because
# this block's CSP is a strict subset of /t*'s, but intentional and worth knowing before editing
# either block.
/tester*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Cache-Control: no-store
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; connect-src https://ftwrvylzoyznhbzhgism.functions.supabase.co; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
